With `--copy-imports`, a refining module can rebind an inherited copying import with another copying import whose target is the previous target or a refinement of it (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/107). Each rebound copy keeps its own type identities. Rebinding must preserve `opened`, every explicitly named export set, and the meaning of inherited names; other forms of redeclaration remain errors. Inherited overrides of the copy's trait members are checked again, and with `--member-invariants`, inherited code is checked against the invariants that the new target adds. The option remains off by default.
